        "subject": "LU-21145 lnet: do not delete Lustre peers on discovery off",
        "message": "LU-21145 lnet: do not delete Lustre peers on discovery off\n\nA client with discovery on can fail to mount with -EIO from servers\nwith discovery off.  The client has two or more networks.\n\nLNetAddPeer() adds the server NIDs as Multi-Rail peers.  A ping reply\nshows that the server has discovery off, and discovery deletes each\npeer.  The next configuration record adds the peer again.  Each delete\ncan move the primary NID, so PtlRPC does not match the reply.\n\nDo not delete a Multi-Rail peer that is not yet discovered.  Only\nLNetAddPeer() makes such a peer, so this rule drops no other case.\nAlso keep a peer with a locked primary NID on a ping reply and on a\npush.  Add conf-sanity test_73m to check that the server peers stay\nMulti-Rail.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 143893381d42 (\"LU-14661 lnet: Check if discovery toggled off in ping reply\")\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ib716349927b6d05f516db71067e886ee5422c3da\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
